  "privacyHeading": "Your Photos, Your Privacy",
  "privacyTitle": "Your photos belong to you.",
  "privacyBody": "Your photos go to a bucket you own, as ordinary files. Next to them is an index.csv that lists every photo by date, album, person, caption and place. With just a spreadsheet, you can find any of them again. No account, no export tool, and no need for us.\n\nThe app only deletes from your bucket to do what you asked: deleting a photo, hiding or unhiding one (the old copy goes once the new one is in every bucket), or a fix you confirm.\n\nNothing is sent to the developer. There's no server and no account. Your library, its records and face data stay in a database on this iPhone, and everything (grouping, search, face recognition) happens here. Photos go only where you send them: your own bucket or your own iCloud.\n\nYour keys are kept in the Keychain, never in the app's own backups. Like everything in the Keychain, they're included in an encrypted iPhone backup.",
