  "settingsBackupFormatFolderNote": "Both formats go in the same \"originals/\" folder in your bucket. Converted photos just end in .heif instead of their original extension.",
  "settingsAppDataHeading": "App Data",
  "settingsAppDataHint": "This covers everything about your library except the photos: albums, people, tags, captions and places.\n\nIt's on for both iCloud Drive and your bucket from the start. Once a day, if anything has changed, a fresh copy is saved. If you reinstall the app, it all comes back on its own.\n\nEach copy also has an index.csv listing every photo by date, album and person, so you can open it without this app.\n\nThis is a backup, not a way to sync between devices. Your bucket keys are never included.",
