  "privateAlbumBackupExplainer": "Hiding a photo removes it from Photos. The app keeps it on this phone in a folder that isn't included in your iPhone backup, under a name that gives nothing away. So the album works without internet or a bucket.\n\nIf you have a bucket, an encrypted copy is uploaded inside a file that opens as an ordinary picture. Only your passphrase and code can open the real photo. That's the copy that survives if you lose this phone or restore it from a backup.\n\nThe app's database keeps a record for each hidden photo, filed under a tag made from its code. That tag can't be turned back into the code without a key stored in your Keychain. App-data backups (Files, iCloud Drive, your bucket) leave hidden photos out, and their notes are encrypted.\n\nTo free up space, select photos in the album to send their full copies to your bucket. Their thumbnails stay, and opening one downloads it again.",
