  "privateAlbumHideNoBucketTitle": "This Phone Will Have the Only Copy",
  "privateAlbumHideAnyway": "Hide Anyway",
  "privateAlbumBackupNoBucket": "Hidden photos are stored encrypted on this phone, so the album works offline.\n\nBut hiding a photo removes it from Photos. Without a bucket, there's no second copy anywhere. If you delete the app, the photo goes with it.",
  "privateAlbumBackupRecentlyDeleted": "Photos keeps deleted items for 30 days. The photo isn't fully hidden until you empty Recently Deleted in Photos.",
  "privateAlbumHowTitle": "How This Works",
  "privateAlbumHowBullets": "Every code opens an album. A code you haven't used opens an empty one, so nothing on this phone shows whether anything is hidden.\nHiding removes the photo from Photos. On this phone, it's kept in a folder that's left out of iPhone backups and has a meaningless name.\nWhat goes to your bucket looks like an ordinary photo: a different picture from your library, with your hidden photo encrypted inside.\nThe decoy is picked to be about the same file size as your photo, so it doesn't stand out.\nThe decoy never carries your photo's date, and nothing records which decoy holds which photo.\nYour passphrase and 4-digit code together make the key. Neither is stored. The key made from your passphrase, and the keys of albums you've opened, are kept in this phone's Keychain so backups can continue without asking you.\nThe database marks hidden photos with a keyed tag derived from the code, never the code itself. App-data backups leave hidden photos out.\nA photo sent back to the bucket keeps its tile here. Thumbnails download 64 KB at a time.\nHiding deletes the photo's unencrypted copy from your bucket, but only after the encrypted copy is in every bucket. Unhiding does the reverse.\nOn a new phone, your passphrase and code bring hidden photos back from the bucket. Hidden photos that never reached a bucket exist only on this phone.\nAnyone who reads this app's source code can spot the disguised photos and count them, but still can't open any of them.",
