  "devWordsHow": "• Made on the Mac from your files and exports.\n• Before importing, you'll see how many of each kind there are. You choose whose writing it is (yours, by default).\n• Each piece has a stable id, so importing a newer file replaces it instead of duplicating it.\n• It shows under Words on the person's page.",
  "devWordsSpec": "File: .zip holding words.jsonl and a media/ folder (or a bare .jsonl).\n\n• Required: id, text (Markdown).\n• title; at (ISO 8601, local; may be a date only).\n• kind: blog, post, essay, fiction, paper, thesis, report, email, note or other.\n• source, origin: where it was published, and the file it came from.\n• Pictures and videos: ![caption](media/<id>/<file>) in text, the file at that path in the zip.",
